From: pocket_vm developers <pocket-vm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] um: vector: define PACKET_QDISC_BYPASS when absent

Qdisc bypass arrived in Linux 3.14 and is a pure optimisation.  On an
older host the constant is simply missing from the headers; with it defined,
the setsockopt fails at runtime instead and the caller falls back to the
queueing path, which is what it already does for any kernel that refuses the
option.
---
 arch/um/drivers/vector_user.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/um/drivers/vector_user.c b/arch/um/drivers/vector_user.c
index 9152bac..eb1ab4e 100644
--- a/arch/um/drivers/vector_user.c
+++ b/arch/um/drivers/vector_user.c
@@ -557,6 +557,16 @@ raw_cleanup:
 }
 
 
+/*
+ * Qdisc bypass arrived in Linux 3.14. On an older host the constant is simply
+ * absent from the headers; the setsockopt below then fails at runtime and the
+ * caller falls back to the queueing path, which is what it already does for
+ * any kernel that refuses the option.
+ */
+#ifndef PACKET_QDISC_BYPASS
+#define PACKET_QDISC_BYPASS 20
+#endif
+
 bool uml_raw_enable_qdisc_bypass(int fd)
 {
 	int optval = 1;
